module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Flat.Stability
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.GradedAlgebra.HomogeneousLocalization
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Localization.Away.Basic
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPolynomial.Homogeneous

/-!
# The standard affine charts of projective space

Grade the polynomial algebra `R[Xⱼ : j ∈ σ]` by total degree and localize homogeneously at one
variable `Xᵢ`. The resulting degree-zero ring
`HomogeneousLocalization.Away (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule σ R) (Xᵢ)` is generated by the
fractions `Xⱼ / Xᵢ` for `j ≠ i`, and those fractions are algebraically independent: the chart is
the polynomial algebra on `σ \ {i}` variables. This is the affine chart `D₊(Xᵢ)` of the projective
space `Proj R[Xⱼ]`, and the symmetric algebra of a free module of rank `r` is exactly this graded
ring for `σ = Fin r`.

Two consequences are recorded. First, the chart is a free, hence flat, module over the ring of
constants, and therefore over the degree-zero part of the grading — which is the ring of constants.
Flatness over the degree-zero part is the hypothesis that
`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.flat_toSpecZero_of_flat_away` asks of each standard chart, so this is the
commutative algebra behind the flatness of a projective bundle over its base. Second, the variables
generate the polynomial algebra over the degree-zero part, which is the covering hypothesis of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.iSup_basicOpen_eq_top'`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SymmetricAway.chartRing R i`: the degree-zero part of the localization of
  `R[Xⱼ : j ∈ σ]` at the variable `Xᵢ`, for the grading by total degree.
* `Stacks.SymmetricAway.mkChart i n p hp`: the fraction `p / Xᵢ ^ n`, for `p` homogeneous of
  degree `n`.
* `Stacks.SymmetricAway.dehomogenize i`: the `R`-algebra map `R[Xⱼ : j ∈ σ] → R[Yⱼ : j ≠ i]`
  setting `Xᵢ = 1`.
* `Stacks.SymmetricAway.toChart i`: the `R`-algebra map `R[Yⱼ : j ≠ i] → chartRing R i` sending
  `Yⱼ` to `Xⱼ / Xᵢ`.
* `Stacks.SymmetricAway.chartAlgEquiv i`: that map, as an isomorphism.
* `Stacks.SymmetricAway.gradeZeroRingEquiv R σ`: the degree-zero part of the grading is the ring
  of constants.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SymmetricAway.chartAlgEquiv`: the chart is an affine space of dimension `#σ - 1` over
  `R`.
* `Stacks.SymmetricAway.flatChartRing`: the chart is a flat module over the degree-zero part of
  the grading.
* `Stacks.SymmetricAway.adjoin_range_X_gradeZero`: the variables generate the polynomial algebra
  over the degree-zero part of the grading.
* `Stacks.SymmetricAway.flat_of_baseRingEquiv`: flatness transfers along an isomorphism of base
  rings.

## Implementation notes

The isomorphism is built from the map *into* the chart, `toChart`, because that map is an
`MvPolynomial.aeval` and so needs no construction. It is surjective because the auxiliary map
`toChartFull`, which sends *every* variable `Xⱼ` to `Xⱼ / Xᵢ` (so `Xᵢ` to `1`), both factors
through `dehomogenize` and sends a homogeneous polynomial `p` of degree `n` to the fraction
`p / Xᵢ ^ n`; `HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk_surjective` says that every element of the chart is
such a fraction. The second of those two facts is the computation
`Stacks.SymmetricAway.fracHom_eq_of_mem`, carried out in the ordinary localization, where the
monomial `∏ Xⱼ ^ dⱼ` contributes `(1 / Xᵢ) ^ ∑ dⱼ`. Injectivity is the left inverse
`chartSpecialize`, which is `dehomogenize` extended to the localization by
`Localization.awayLift`, legitimately because `dehomogenize` sends `Xᵢ` to the unit `1`.

The degree-zero part of the grading is the submodule of constants, and the coefficient ring acts
on the chart through it (`Stacks.SymmetricAway.algebraChartRing`). Flatness is proved over the
coefficient ring, where freeness is immediate from the isomorphism, and transported along
`gradeZeroRingEquiv`; `flat_of_baseRingEquiv` is the transport, which the library did not have.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached: nothing here is one of the assertions of a Stacks tag. The
flatness of a projective bundle is part of tag 02TX, whose statement is about the relative `Proj`
of a symmetric algebra; this is one input to it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02TX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02TX)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open MvPolynomial HomogeneousLocalization

namespace Stacks.SymmetricAway

attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.gradedAlgebra

universe u v

variable {σ : Type v} {R : Type u} [CommRing R]

/-! ### The chart ring and its elements -/

/-- A variable is homogeneous of degree one for the grading by total degree. -/
theorem X_mem_homogeneousSubmodule_one (i : σ) :
    (X i : MvPolynomial σ R) ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R 1 :=
  (mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).2 (isHomogeneous_X R i)

/-- The standard affine chart ring of projective space: the degree-zero part of the localization
of `R[Xⱼ : j ∈ σ]` at the variable `Xᵢ`, for the grading by total degree. -/
abbrev chartRing (R : Type u) [CommRing R] {σ : Type v} (i : σ) : Type (max u v) :=
  HomogeneousLocalization.Away (homogeneousSubmodule σ R) (X i)

/-- The coefficient ring acts on the chart ring through the degree-zero part of the grading. -/
instance algebraChartRing (i : σ) : Algebra R (chartRing R i) :=
  ((algebraMap (homogeneousSubmodule σ R 0) (chartRing R i)).comp
    (algebraMap R (homogeneousSubmodule σ R 0))).toAlgebra

/-- The fraction `p / Xᵢ ^ n`, for `p` homogeneous of degree `n`. -/
def mkChart (i : σ) (n : ℕ) (p : MvPolynomial σ R) (hp : p ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R n) :
    chartRing R i :=
  Away.mk _ (X_mem_homogeneousSubmodule_one i) n p (by simpa using hp)

/-- The fraction `p / Xᵢ ^ n` of the chart ring, read in the ordinary localization. -/
theorem val_mkChart (i : σ) (n : ℕ) (p : MvPolynomial σ R)
    (hp : p ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R n) :
    (mkChart i n p hp).val =
      Localization.mk p (⟨X i ^ n, n, rfl⟩ : Submonoid.powers (X i : MvPolynomial σ R)) := rfl

/-! ### Inverting a variable in the ordinary localization -/

/-- The inverse of `Xᵢ` in the localization away from `Xᵢ`. -/
def invX (i : σ) : Localization.Away (X i : MvPolynomial σ R) :=
  Localization.mk 1 ⟨X i, 1, pow_one _⟩

/-- The powers of the inverse of `Xᵢ`. -/
theorem invX_pow (i : σ) (n : ℕ) :
    (invX (R := R) i) ^ n =
      Localization.mk 1 (⟨X i ^ n, n, rfl⟩ : Submonoid.powers (X i : MvPolynomial σ R)) := by
  rw [invX, Localization.mk_pow, one_pow]
  congr 1

/-- The inverse of `Xᵢ` is a right inverse of `Xᵢ`. -/
theorem algebraMap_X_mul_invX (i : σ) :
    algebraMap (MvPolynomial σ R) (Localization.Away (X i : MvPolynomial σ R)) (X i) * invX i
      = 1 := by
  rw [invX, ← Localization.mk_one_eq_algebraMap, Localization.mk_mul, mul_one, one_mul]
  exact Localization.mk_self (⟨X i, 1, pow_one _⟩ : Submonoid.powers (X i : MvPolynomial σ R))

/-- A fraction with denominator a power of `Xᵢ`, rewritten using the inverse of `Xᵢ`. -/
theorem localization_mk_eq (i : σ) (p : MvPolynomial σ R) (n : ℕ) :
    Localization.mk p (⟨X i ^ n, n, rfl⟩ : Submonoid.powers (X i : MvPolynomial σ R)) =
      algebraMap (MvPolynomial σ R) _ p * invX i ^ n := by
  rw [invX_pow, ← Localization.mk_one_eq_algebraMap, Localization.mk_mul, mul_one, one_mul]

/-! ### Dehomogenization -/

/-- Dehomogenization at `Xᵢ`: the `R`-algebra map sending `Xᵢ` to `1` and `Xⱼ` to the `j`-th
variable of the polynomial algebra on the remaining indices. -/
def dehomogenize (i : σ) : MvPolynomial σ R →ₐ[R] MvPolynomial {j : σ // j ≠ i} R :=
  MvPolynomial.aeval fun j =>
    letI : Decidable (j = i) := Classical.dec _
    if h : j = i then (1 : MvPolynomial {j : σ // j ≠ i} R) else X ⟨j, h⟩

/-- Dehomogenization sends the chosen variable to `1`. -/
@[simp] theorem dehomogenize_X_self (i : σ) : dehomogenize (R := R) i (X i) = 1 := by
  simp [dehomogenize]

/-- Dehomogenization keeps every other variable. -/
@[simp] theorem dehomogenize_X_of_ne {i j : σ} (h : j ≠ i) :
    dehomogenize (R := R) i (X j) = X ⟨j, h⟩ := by
  simp [dehomogenize, h]

/-- Dehomogenization is the identity on constants. -/
@[simp] theorem dehomogenize_C (i : σ) (r : R) :
    dehomogenize (R := R) i (C r) = C r := by
  simp [dehomogenize]

/-! ### The fractions `Xⱼ / Xᵢ` in the ordinary localization -/

/-- The `R`-algebra map `Xⱼ ↦ Xⱼ / Xᵢ` into the localization away from `Xᵢ`. -/
def fracHom (i : σ) : MvPolynomial σ R →ₐ[R] Localization.Away (X i : MvPolynomial σ R) :=
  MvPolynomial.aeval fun j =>
    algebraMap (MvPolynomial σ R) (Localization.Away (X i : MvPolynomial σ R)) (X j) * invX i

/-- The value of `fracHom` on a variable. -/
theorem fracHom_X (i j : σ) :
    fracHom (R := R) i (X j) =
      algebraMap (MvPolynomial σ R) (Localization.Away (X i : MvPolynomial σ R)) (X j) *
        invX i := by
  simp [fracHom]

/-- The value of `fracHom` on a constant. -/
@[simp] theorem fracHom_C (i : σ) (r : R) :
    fracHom (R := R) i (C r)
      = algebraMap R (Localization.Away (X i : MvPolynomial σ R)) r := by
  simp [fracHom]

/-- A constant polynomial and the constant itself have the same image in the localization. -/
private theorem algebraMap_C_away (i : σ) (r : R) :
    algebraMap (MvPolynomial σ R) (Localization.Away (X i : MvPolynomial σ R)) (C r)
      = algebraMap R _ r := by
  rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R (MvPolynomial σ R) _ r, algebraMap_eq]

/-- The value of `fracHom` on a monomial: each of the `∑ dⱼ` variables contributes one factor
`1 / Xᵢ`. -/
theorem fracHom_monomial (i : σ) (d : σ →₀ ℕ) (c : R) :
    fracHom i (monomial d c) =
      algebraMap (MvPolynomial σ R) _ (monomial d c) * invX i ^ d.degree := by
  rw [fracHom, aeval_monomial, monomial_eq, map_mul, map_finsuppProd,
    algebraMap_C_away, Finsupp.prod, Finsupp.prod, Finsupp.degree_apply,
    ← Finset.prod_pow_eq_pow_sum, mul_assoc]
  congr 1
  rw [← Finset.prod_mul_distrib]
  exact Finset.prod_congr rfl fun k _ => by rw [mul_pow, map_pow]

/-- **A homogeneous polynomial of degree `n` is `Xᵢ ^ n` times the value of `fracHom` on it.**
Dividing by `Xᵢ ^ n` makes the fractions `Xⱼ / Xᵢ` compute the chart. -/
theorem fracHom_eq_of_mem (i : σ) (n : ℕ) (p : MvPolynomial σ R)
    (hp : p ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R n) :
    fracHom i p = algebraMap (MvPolynomial σ R) _ p * invX i ^ n := by
  conv_lhs => rw [p.as_sum]
  conv_rhs => rw [p.as_sum]
  rw [map_sum, map_sum, Finset.sum_mul]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun d hd => ?_
  have hdeg : d.degree = n := by
    by_contra hne
    exact (mem_support_iff.mp hd) (((mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).1 hp).coeff_eq_zero hne)
  rw [fracHom_monomial, hdeg]

/-! ### The chart is an affine space -/

/-- A constant, read in the ordinary localization. -/
theorem val_algebraMap_eq (i : σ) (r : R) :
    (algebraMap R (chartRing R i) r).val
      = algebraMap (MvPolynomial σ R) (Localization.Away (X i : MvPolynomial σ R)) (C r) := by
  rw [← Localization.mk_one_eq_algebraMap]
  rfl

/-- The fraction `Xᵢ / Xᵢ` is `1`. -/
theorem mkChart_X_self (i : σ) :
    mkChart (R := R) i 1 (X i) (X_mem_homogeneousSubmodule_one i) = 1 := by
  apply HomogeneousLocalization.val_injective
  rw [val_mkChart, HomogeneousLocalization.val_one, localization_mk_eq, pow_one,
    algebraMap_X_mul_invX]

/-- A constant is the fraction `C r / Xᵢ ^ 0`. -/
theorem algebraMap_eq_mkChart (i : σ) (r : R) :
    algebraMap R (chartRing R i) r = mkChart i 0 (C r) ((mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).2
      (isHomogeneous_C _ r)) := by
  apply HomogeneousLocalization.val_injective
  rw [val_mkChart, localization_mk_eq, pow_zero, mul_one, val_algebraMap_eq]

/-- The comparison of the affine space on the variables other than `Xᵢ` with the chart:
`Yⱼ ↦ Xⱼ / Xᵢ`. -/
def toChart (i : σ) : MvPolynomial {j : σ // j ≠ i} R →ₐ[R] chartRing R i :=
  MvPolynomial.aeval fun j => mkChart i 1 (X j.1) (X_mem_homogeneousSubmodule_one j.1)

/-- The comparison map sends a variable to a fraction of variables. -/
@[simp] theorem toChart_X (i : σ) (j : {j : σ // j ≠ i}) :
    toChart (R := R) i (X j) = mkChart i 1 (X j.1) (X_mem_homogeneousSubmodule_one j.1) := by
  simp [toChart]

/-- The comparison map is the identity on constants. -/
@[simp] theorem toChart_C (i : σ) (r : R) :
    toChart (R := R) i (C r) = algebraMap R (chartRing R i) r := by
  simp [toChart]

/-- The variant of `Stacks.SymmetricAway.toChart` defined on *every* variable, sending `Xⱼ` to
`Xⱼ / Xᵢ` and hence `Xᵢ` to `1`. -/
def toChartFull (i : σ) : MvPolynomial σ R →ₐ[R] chartRing R i :=
  MvPolynomial.aeval fun j => mkChart i 1 (X j) (X_mem_homogeneousSubmodule_one j)

/-- The value of `toChartFull` on a variable. -/
@[simp] theorem toChartFull_X (i j : σ) :
    toChartFull (R := R) i (X j) = mkChart i 1 (X j) (X_mem_homogeneousSubmodule_one j) := by
  simp [toChartFull]

/-- The value of `toChartFull` on a constant. -/
@[simp] theorem toChartFull_C (i : σ) (r : R) :
    toChartFull (R := R) i (C r) = algebraMap R (chartRing R i) r := by
  simp [toChartFull]

/-- `toChartFull` is `fracHom` read in the chart. -/
theorem val_toChartFull (i : σ) (p : MvPolynomial σ R) :
    (toChartFull i p).val = fracHom i p := by
  have key : (algebraMap (chartRing R i)
        (Localization.Away (X i : MvPolynomial σ R))).comp (toChartFull i).toRingHom
      = (fracHom i).toRingHom := by
    refine MvPolynomial.ringHom_ext ?_ ?_
    · intro r
      show ((toChartFull i) (C r)).val = fracHom i (C r)
      rw [toChartFull_C, fracHom_C, val_algebraMap_eq, algebraMap_C_away]
    · intro j
      show ((toChartFull i) (X j)).val = fracHom i (X j)
      rw [toChartFull_X, val_mkChart, fracHom_X, localization_mk_eq, pow_one]
  exact RingHom.congr_fun key p

/-- **`toChartFull` sends a homogeneous polynomial of degree `n` to its quotient by `Xᵢ ^ n`.** -/
theorem toChartFull_eq_mkChart (i : σ) (n : ℕ) (p : MvPolynomial σ R)
    (hp : p ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R n) :
    toChartFull i p = mkChart i n p hp := by
  apply HomogeneousLocalization.val_injective
  rw [val_toChartFull, val_mkChart, localization_mk_eq, fracHom_eq_of_mem i n p hp]

/-- `toChartFull` factors through dehomogenization. -/
theorem toChartFull_eq_comp (i : σ) :
    toChartFull (R := R) i = (toChart i).comp (dehomogenize i) := by
  refine MvPolynomial.algHom_ext fun j => ?_
  rw [AlgHom.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply, toChartFull_X]
  by_cases h : j = i
  · subst h
    rw [mkChart_X_self, dehomogenize_X_self, map_one]
  · rw [dehomogenize_X_of_ne h, toChart_X]

/-- `toChartFull` factors through dehomogenization, pointwise. -/
theorem toChart_dehomogenize (i : σ) (p : MvPolynomial σ R) :
    toChart i (dehomogenize i p) = toChartFull i p := by
  rw [toChartFull_eq_comp, AlgHom.comp_apply]

/-- **The fractions `Xⱼ / Xᵢ` generate the chart.** Every element of the chart is a quotient
`p / Xᵢ ^ n` with `p` homogeneous of degree `n`, and dehomogenizing `p` names it. -/
theorem toChart_surjective (i : σ) : Function.Surjective (toChart (R := R) i) := by
  intro z
  obtain ⟨n, p, hp, hz⟩ :=
    Away.mk_surjective (homogeneousSubmodule σ R) (X_mem_homogeneousSubmodule_one i) z
  refine ⟨dehomogenize i p, ?_⟩
  rwa [toChart_dehomogenize, toChartFull_eq_mkChart i n p (by simpa using hp)]

/-- The inverse of `Stacks.SymmetricAway.toChart`: dehomogenization, extended to the chart.
It is defined because dehomogenization sends `Xᵢ` to the unit `1`. -/
def chartSpecialize (i : σ) : chartRing R i →+* MvPolynomial {j : σ // j ≠ i} R :=
  (Localization.awayLift (dehomogenize (R := R) i).toRingHom (X i)
      (isUnit_iff_exists_inv.mpr ⟨1, by simp⟩)).comp
    (algebraMap (chartRing R i) (Localization.Away (X i : MvPolynomial σ R)))

/-- Dehomogenization forgets the denominator of a fraction of the chart. -/
theorem chartSpecialize_mkChart (i : σ) (n : ℕ) (p : MvPolynomial σ R)
    (hp : p ∈ homogeneousSubmodule σ R n) :
    chartSpecialize i (mkChart i n p hp) = dehomogenize i p := by
  rw [chartSpecialize, RingHom.comp_apply]
  show Localization.awayLift _ _ _ (mkChart i n p hp).val = _
  rw [val_mkChart,
    Localization.awayLift_mk (dehomogenize (R := R) i).toRingHom (X i) p 1 (by simp) n,
    one_pow, mul_one]
  rfl

/-- **The fractions `Xⱼ / Xᵢ` are algebraically independent.** -/
theorem chartSpecialize_toChart (i : σ) (q : MvPolynomial {j : σ // j ≠ i} R) :
    chartSpecialize i (toChart i q) = q := by
  have key : (chartSpecialize (R := R) i).comp (toChart i).toRingHom
      = RingHom.id (MvPolynomial {j : σ // j ≠ i} R) := by
    refine MvPolynomial.ringHom_ext ?_ ?_
    · intro r
      show chartSpecialize i (toChart i (C r)) = C r
      rw [toChart_C, algebraMap_eq_mkChart, chartSpecialize_mkChart, dehomogenize_C]
    · intro j
      show chartSpecialize i (toChart i (X j)) = X j
      rw [toChart_X, chartSpecialize_mkChart, dehomogenize_X_of_ne j.2]
  exact RingHom.congr_fun key q

/-- **The standard affine chart of projective space is an affine space.** For the grading of
`R[Xⱼ : j ∈ σ]` by total degree and a variable `Xᵢ`, the degree-zero part of the localization at
`Xᵢ` is freely generated as an `R`-algebra by the fractions `Xⱼ / Xᵢ` for `j ≠ i`. -/
def chartAlgEquiv (i : σ) : MvPolynomial {j : σ // j ≠ i} R ≃ₐ[R] chartRing R i :=
  AlgEquiv.ofBijective (toChart i)
    ⟨Function.LeftInverse.injective (chartSpecialize_toChart i), toChart_surjective i⟩

/-- The chart isomorphism is `Stacks.SymmetricAway.toChart`. -/
@[simp] theorem chartAlgEquiv_apply (i : σ) (q : MvPolynomial {j : σ // j ≠ i} R) :
    chartAlgEquiv i q = toChart i q := rfl

/-- The chart is a free module over the coefficient ring. -/
instance freeChartRing (i : σ) : Module.Free R (chartRing R i) :=
  Module.Free.of_equiv (chartAlgEquiv (R := R) i).toLinearEquiv

/-! ### Flatness over the degree-zero part of the grading -/

/-- **Flatness transfers along an isomorphism of base rings.** A module carrying actions of two
isomorphic rings which agree through the isomorphism is flat over one as soon as it is flat over
the other. -/
theorem flat_of_baseRingEquiv {A B M : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module A M] [Module B M] (e : A ≃+* B)
    (he : ∀ (b : B) (m : M), b • m = e.symm b • m) [Module.Flat A M] :
    Module.Flat B M := by
  let _ : Algebra B A := e.symm.toRingHom.toAlgebra
  have hsmul : ∀ (b : B) (a : A), b • a = e.symm b * a := fun b a => Algebra.smul_def b a
  have : Module.Flat B A := by
    refine Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv (R := B) (M := B) (N := A) (LinearEquiv.ofBijective
      ({ toFun := e, map_add' := map_add e,
          map_smul' := fun b a => by
            show e (b • a) = b • e a
            rw [hsmul, map_mul, RingEquiv.apply_symm_apply, smul_eq_mul] } : A →ₗ[B] B)
      ⟨e.injective, e.surjective⟩)
  have : IsScalarTower B A M := ⟨fun b a m => by rw [hsmul, mul_smul, he]⟩
  exact Module.Flat.trans B A M

/-- **The degree-zero part of the grading by total degree is the ring of constants.** -/
def gradeZeroRingEquiv (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (σ : Type v) :
    R ≃+* (homogeneousSubmodule σ R 0) :=
  RingEquiv.ofBijective (algebraMap R (homogeneousSubmodule σ R 0))
    ⟨fun r r' h => C_injective σ R (by
        simpa only [SetLike.GradeZero.coe_algebraMap, algebraMap_eq] using congrArg Subtype.val h),
      fun x => by
        have hx : (x : MvPolynomial σ R) ∈ (1 : Submodule R (MvPolynomial σ R)) := by
          rw [← homogeneousSubmodule_zero]
          exact x.2
        obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := Submodule.mem_one.1 hx
        exact ⟨r, Subtype.ext (by
          simpa only [SetLike.GradeZero.coe_algebraMap] using hr)⟩⟩

/-- The identification of the degree-zero part with the coefficient ring is the structure map. -/
theorem gradeZeroRingEquiv_apply (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (σ : Type v) (r : R) :
    gradeZeroRingEquiv R σ r = algebraMap R (homogeneousSubmodule σ R 0) r := rfl

/-- **The standard affine chart of projective space is flat over the degree-zero part of the
grading.** This is the sole piece of commutative algebra behind the flatness of a projective
bundle over its base: it is the hypothesis `hflat` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.flat_toSpecZero_of_flat_away` for the grading by total degree. -/
instance flatChartRing (i : σ) :
    Module.Flat (homogeneousSubmodule σ R 0) (chartRing R i) := by
  refine flat_of_baseRingEquiv (gradeZeroRingEquiv R σ) fun b z => ?_
  have key : algebraMap R (chartRing R i) ((gradeZeroRingEquiv R σ).symm b)
      = algebraMap (homogeneousSubmodule σ R 0) (chartRing R i) b := by
    rw [show algebraMap R (chartRing R i) = (algebraMap (homogeneousSubmodule σ R 0)
        (chartRing R i)).comp (algebraMap R (homogeneousSubmodule σ R 0)) from rfl,
      RingHom.comp_apply, ← gradeZeroRingEquiv_apply, RingEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
  rw [Algebra.smul_def, Algebra.smul_def, key]

/-! ### The variables cover `Proj` -/

/-- **The variables generate the polynomial algebra over the degree-zero part of the grading.**
This is the hypothesis of `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.iSup_basicOpen_eq_top'` which says that the
standard opens `D₊(Xᵢ)` cover `Proj R[Xⱼ]`. -/
theorem adjoin_range_X_gradeZero (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (σ : Type v) :
    Algebra.adjoin (homogeneousSubmodule σ R 0)
      (Set.range (X : σ → MvPolynomial σ R)) = ⊤ := by
  refine Algebra.eq_top_iff.2 fun p => ?_
  induction p using MvPolynomial.induction_on with
  | C r =>
      exact (Algebra.adjoin (homogeneousSubmodule σ R 0)
        (Set.range (X : σ → MvPolynomial σ R))).algebraMap_mem
          ⟨C r, (mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).2 (isHomogeneous_C _ r)⟩
  | add p q hp hq => exact (Algebra.adjoin _ _).add_mem hp hq
  | mul_X p i hp => exact (Algebra.adjoin _ _).mul_mem hp (Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨i, rfl⟩)

end Stacks.SymmetricAway

